    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **261 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement in the owner create endpoint (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, which handles `POST /api/owners`):\n\n1. Added a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n   ```\n\n2. After the owner is successfully persisted (`saveOwner`), emit one audit line carrying the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`:\n   ```java\n   this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);\n   AUDIT.info(\"owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nThe line is emitted only on the success path (after all validation/quota/duplicate checks pass and the entity is saved), so failed creates produce no audit line. The `registrationDate` is logged via `LocalDate`'s ISO-8601 `toString()`, matching the value the DTO serializes and the test reads back from `GET /api/owners/{id}`. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
